Code
library(tidyverse)

orders &lt;- read_csv("data/orders.csv")
order_items &lt;- read_csv("data/order_items.csv")
products &lt;- read_csv("data/products.csv")
sellers &lt;- read_csv("data/sellers.csv")

orders_clean &lt;- orders |&gt;
  filter(order_status == "delivered") |&gt;
  filter(!is.na(delivery_days)) |&gt;
  mutate(
    delivery_status = if_else(
      delivery_days &lt;= estimated_days,
      "On Time",
      "Late"
    )
  )

supply_chain_data &lt;- orders_clean |&gt;
  left_join(order_items, by = "order_id") |&gt;
  left_join(sellers, by = "seller_id") |&gt;
  left_join(products, by = "product_id") |&gt;
  mutate(
    freight_ratio = freight_value / price
  )
This exploration examines how seller scale, delivery performance, freight cost, and product characteristics interact across the marketplace.
The goal is to identify which seller groups are supporting efficient marketplace growth and which groups may require more operational attention.
Business question: Which seller segments are helping the marketplace scale efficiently, and which ones are creating high fulfillment costs or weak operational performance?

Building the analytical dataset
The cleaned order data is then joined with order-item, seller, and product information.


